# 🎯 Interview Cheat Sheet

Memorize these definitions:

> **RPS:** Number of requests handled per second.
> 

> **Latency:** Time taken to complete one request/operation.
> 

> **Throughput:** Amount of work processed per unit of time.
> 

> **Availability:** How often the system is accessible and operational.
> 

> **Scalability:** Ability to handle increasing load by adding resources.
> 

> **Reliability:** Ability to consistently perform correctly over time.
> 

> **Durability:** Ability to preserve data without loss.
> 

> **Consistency:** How data appears across system components/replicas according to defined guarantees.
> 

> **Fault tolerance:** Ability to continue operating despite component failures.
> 

> **SPOF:** A single component whose failure can bring down the system.
> 

> **Horizontal scaling:** Add more machines/instances.
> 

> **Vertical scaling:** Increase resources of an existing machine.
> 

> **Stateless:** Server does not depend on locally stored session/application state between requests.
> 

> **Bottleneck:** Component limiting overall system performance.
> 

> **Trade-off:** Choosing one desirable property at the cost of another.
> 

### The most important mental model

```
          LOAD
           │
           ▼
     Capacity Planning
           │
           ▼
    ┌───────────────┐
    │ Architecture  │
    └───────────────┘
       │    │    │
