> 
> **Timeout**
> 
> > "A timeout prevents a service from waiting indefinitely for a dependency and protects resources such as connections and workers."
> > 
> 
> **Retry**
> 
> > "I retry only transient failures, with a bounded retry count and exponential backoff with jitter."
> > 
> 
> **Circuit breaker**
> 
> > "A circuit breaker stops calls to a repeatedly failing dependency, allowing it time to recover and preventing cascading failures."
> > 
> 
> **Bulkhead**
> 
> > "Bulkheads isolate resources between workloads so one overloaded dependency cannot exhaust the resources of the entire application."
> > 
> 
> **Graceful degradation**
> 
> > "When a non-critical dependency fails, the system continues providing core functionality with reduced features."
> > 
> 
> **Authentication**
> 
> > "Authentication verifies who the user is."
> > 
> 
> **Authorization**
> 
> > "Authorization determines what an authenticated user is allowed to do."
> > 
> 
> **OAuth 2.0 vs OIDC**
> 
> > "OAuth 2.0 is primarily an authorization framework, while OpenID Connect adds authentication and identity on top of OAuth 2.0."
> > 
> 
> **CORS**
> 
> > "CORS is a browser security mechanism that controls which origins are allowed to make cross-origin requests to a server."
> > 
> 
> **Secrets**
> 
> > "Credentials and secrets should never be hardcoded or committed to Git. They should be stored in a dedicated secret-management system and accessed using appropriate identity and permissions."
> > 
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 🔥 The Big Picture
> 
> At this point your system-design knowledge is starting to connect:
> 
> ```
>                          USERS
>                            │
>                            ▼
>                     CDN / WAF / TLS
>                            │
>                            ▼
>                     Rate Limiting
>                            │
>                            ▼
>                          ALB
>                            │
>              ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
>              ▼             ▼             ▼
>             API           API           API
>              │             │             │
>              └─────────────┼─────────────┘
>                            │
>                   ┌────────┼────────┐
>                   ▼        ▼        ▼
>                 Redis     RDS      Queue
>                   │        │        │
>                   │        │        ▼
>                   │        │      Workers
>                   │        │        │
>                   │        │        ▼
>                   │        │       DLQ
>                   │        │
>                   │    Replicas
>                   │        │
>                   └────────┘
> 
> Reliability:
> Timeout → Retry → Backoff → Jitter → Circuit Breaker
>                                       ↓
>                               Graceful Degradation
> 
> Security:
> Authentication → Authorization → RBAC → Permissions
>        │
>        ├── OAuth/OIDC
>        ├── Access/Refresh Tokens
>        └── Secrets Management
> ```
> 
> **This is the mental model you should carry into system-design interviews:** don't just name AWS services or patterns. Explain **what failure/problem exists → which pattern solves it → what trade-off that pattern introduces**.
