# 7. CloudFront ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Amazon Web Services CloudFront is AWS's CDN service.

Typical architecture:

```
                    User
                      │
                      ▼
                  CloudFront
                      │
             ┌────────┴────────┐
             ▼                 ▼
            S3               ALB
         Static files      Dynamic API
```

Example:

```
React/Next.js static assets
             ↓
             S3
             ↓
         CloudFront
```

API:

```
User
 ↓
CloudFront
 ↓
ALB
 ↓
ECS
 ↓
FastAPI/Node.js
```

---

# CDN + Cache + API

Be careful here.

Not every API response should be cached.

Static:

```
logo.png
app.js
style.css
```

✅ Excellent CDN candidates.

Public product catalog:

```
GET /products
```

✅ Potentially cacheable with correct rules.

Private user data:

```
GET /my-account
```

❌ Usually should not be publicly cached.

Payment:

```
POST /payment
```

❌ Don't treat it like a static cacheable resource.

