**Monolithic Architecture**

Monolithic architecture is a software design pattern where the entire web application — including the **frontend, backend, and database layer** — is built and maintained within a **single codebase, single repository, and deployed as one unit**. All components are tightly integrated and run as one centralized system. Instead of separating services, everything is developed and managed together.

