### 3. Columnar (Wide-Column) Database

A **Columnar DB** stores data in columns instead of rows. It is optimized for large-scale data and analytics queries.

**Use Case:**

Best for big data, analytics platforms, logging systems, time-series data.

**Example:**

Store IoT sensor data where each column represents temperature, voltage, current, etc.

